1
00:00:01,835 --> 00:00:05,339
Is anyone else troubled
by the Spider-Man theme song?

2
00:00:06,465 --> 00:00:09,760
Why would it trouble you?
It's your third-favorite cartoon theme song.

3
00:00:09,927 --> 00:00:14,264
It is, right behind,
"Do, do, do, do, do, Inspector Gadget."

4
00:00:15,641 --> 00:00:20,103
And Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles.
Heroes in a half shell.

5
00:00:20,354 --> 00:00:22,231
Turtle power.

6
00:00:22,773 --> 00:00:26,777
However, the Spider-Man lyrics posit
that Spider-Man, Spider-Man...

7
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:30,072
-...does whatever a spider can.
-Yeah, so?

8
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:33,784
I can think of many things
Spider-Man can't do that a spider can.

9
00:00:33,951 --> 00:00:36,161
One, crawl in your ear and die.

10
00:00:37,079 --> 00:00:40,123
Two, legally leave Guatemala
without a passport.

11
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:43,460
And three, have sex with a spider.

12
00:00:44,419 --> 00:00:48,966
Can we change the subject?
Spiders give me the jeebie-jeebies.

13
00:00:49,967 --> 00:00:51,802
It's "heebie-jeebies."

14
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:54,888
I know, but that sounds anti-Semitic.

15
00:00:56,765 --> 00:00:59,476
I was thinking we could have
a little film festival tonight.

16
00:00:59,685 --> 00:01:02,479
The theme:
Movies that killed their franchises.

17
00:01:02,646 --> 00:01:08,527
Oh.
Like Jaws 4, Indiana Jones 4, Daredevil 1.

18
00:01:09,820 --> 00:01:12,489
Miss Congeniality 2: Armed and Fabulous.

19
00:01:12,698 --> 00:01:17,911
I mean, you know a movie's bad
when my homegirl Sandy B can't save it.

20
00:01:19,454 --> 00:01:20,998
Penny's working tonight. I'm in.

21
00:01:21,206 --> 00:01:24,668
Not me. I'm having dinner with Bernadette
and her parents.

22
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:27,671
-Fun. We know how much you love that.
HOWARD: It's torture.

23
00:01:27,838 --> 00:01:30,674
Especially with her dad.
We have nothing in common.

24
00:01:30,841 --> 00:01:33,844
You know what I like to do
when I'm forced to speak with those...

25
00:01:34,052 --> 00:01:36,430
...beneath my intellectual station?

26
00:01:36,638 --> 00:01:38,473
I bring up an interesting topic...

27
00:01:38,682 --> 00:01:42,728
...like the difference between
Spider-Man and spiders.

28
00:01:44,521 --> 00:01:47,024
Thanks, Sheldon.
I'll try that with my father-in-law.

29
00:01:47,232 --> 00:01:49,151
No, you can't use that one. That's mine.

30
00:01:49,359 --> 00:01:50,694
Try this one for an icebreaker.

31
00:01:50,861 --> 00:01:52,529
Uh, despite popular lore...

32
00:01:52,696 --> 00:01:56,533
...there is no place in the continental
United States, Alaska or Hawaii...

33
00:01:56,742 --> 00:02:01,038
...from which one can dig straight through
the center of the Earth and come up in China.

34
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:05,083
Great. Thank you.

35
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:08,378
Actually, you can't have that one either.
It's too good. Sorry.

36
00:02:08,587 --> 00:02:10,547
What about you, Sheldon?
Do you have plans?

37
00:02:10,756 --> 00:02:14,551
Sadly, yes. Amy's taking me
to a memorial service.

38
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:17,512
It's for one of her colleagues
who is of Asian descent...

39
00:02:17,721 --> 00:02:20,849
...so my planned conversational gambit
is to casually remark...

40
00:02:21,058 --> 00:02:26,104
...that no matter how deep they dig his grave,
he'll never make his way back to China.

41
00:02:28,398 --> 00:02:30,525
That should lighten the mood.

42
00:02:30,734 --> 00:02:33,487
What can I say, I put the "fun" in funeral.

43
00:02:59,721 --> 00:03:01,098
Amy? Amy?

44
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:02,599
The Fish Guts Displacement

45
00:03:02,766 --> 00:03:04,267
Oh, right, funeral.

46
00:03:04,518 --> 00:03:06,061
Amy?

47
00:03:08,438 --> 00:03:09,815
Hello, Sheldon.

48
00:03:10,065 --> 00:03:12,234
I'm not allowed to wear
my Silver Surfer tie...

49
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:15,070
...but you can wear a bathrobe?

50
00:03:15,404 --> 00:03:17,322
I think I'm too sick to go to the funeral.

51
00:03:17,781 --> 00:03:20,450
You're sick? You poor kid.

52
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:22,452
Well, see you.

53
00:03:22,953 --> 00:03:25,455
Sheldon, aren't you gonna take care of me?

54
00:03:25,622 --> 00:03:29,459
Me? No, I'm not that kind of doctor.

55
00:03:30,419 --> 00:03:32,587
But our relationship agreement
clearly states...

56
00:03:32,796 --> 00:03:35,590
...when one of us is sick,
the other must take care of them.

57
00:03:35,757 --> 00:03:38,301
Oh. I see the confusion.

58
00:03:38,468 --> 00:03:43,974
The intent behind that clause
was to force you to take care of me when I'm ill.

59
00:03:45,183 --> 00:03:48,311
When you're feeling better,
you'll think that's funny.

60
00:03:51,773 --> 00:03:53,442
Never mind. Good night, Sheldon.

61
00:04:03,785 --> 00:04:07,330
Amy? Amy? Amy?

62
00:04:09,708 --> 00:04:12,711
I made a commitment in writing
to comfort you in times like this.

63
00:04:12,961 --> 00:04:16,798
And, additionally, you are my girlfriend
and I care about your well-being.

64
00:04:19,468 --> 00:04:21,803
-Thank you, Sheldon.
-You're welcome.

65
00:04:22,012 --> 00:04:23,972
Now let's get this over with.

66
00:04:37,194 --> 00:04:40,030
-So how have you been?
-Fine.

67
00:04:40,197 --> 00:04:41,823
Good.

68
00:04:42,324 --> 00:04:43,992
Fine is good.

69
00:04:53,210 --> 00:04:56,713
-How are you liking retirement?
-It's fine.

70
00:04:58,715 --> 00:05:00,133
I'm sensing a theme.

71
00:05:05,847 --> 00:05:10,060
You ever really think about
the Spider-Man theme song?

72
00:05:12,354 --> 00:05:13,647
How's that dinner coming?

73
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:19,528
-I just put it in. It's gonna be a while.
-I like rare chicken. Let's do this.

74
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:21,738
You could die.

75
00:05:26,159 --> 00:05:31,081
Death by chicken. Ha, ha.
That's a pretty fowl way to go.

76
00:05:36,545 --> 00:05:39,965
-Here's another beer, honey.
-Thank you.

77
00:05:40,215 --> 00:05:44,261
So, Mrs. Rostenkowski,
you took that trip to the Grand Canyon.

78
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:48,098
-How was it?
-It was good.

79
00:05:52,227 --> 00:05:54,688
Had no idea you were the chatty one.

80
00:05:58,149 --> 00:05:59,192
[THERMOMETER BEEPS]

81
00:06:03,071 --> 00:06:04,447
One hundred two point two.

82
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:05,657
[COUGHS]

83
00:06:06,241 --> 00:06:09,119
Exactly what it was half an hour ago.

84
00:06:09,411 --> 00:06:11,746
It's like you're not even trying to get better.

85
00:06:14,416 --> 00:06:17,210
Sheldon, you don't get over the flu
in half an hour.

86
00:06:17,419 --> 00:06:18,920
Well, not with that attitude.

87
00:06:20,422 --> 00:06:24,467
You know, I have to say,
I'm finding your bedside manner a little lacking.

88
00:06:24,718 --> 00:06:27,929
I'm sorry. I just want you to get better
as soon as possible.

89
00:06:28,471 --> 00:06:32,142
And with that goal in mind,
let me ask you a question.

90
00:06:32,350 --> 00:06:34,811
Do you believe in the placebo effect?

91
00:06:34,978 --> 00:06:38,231
Of course I do. There have been many studies
proving its validity.

92
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:43,361
Great. Now, this may look like a Tic Tac...

93
00:06:44,738 --> 00:06:49,034
...but it is really a powerful medication
specifically designed...

94
00:06:49,284 --> 00:06:52,787
...to cure your illness,
as well as freshen your breath.

95
00:06:53,622 --> 00:06:55,957
Sheldon, this isn't helping.

96
00:06:56,166 --> 00:06:58,001
Why don't you just let me get some rest?

97
00:06:58,168 --> 00:07:01,171
How can you sleep?
I'm not done making you feel better.

98
00:07:01,379 --> 00:07:05,884
I still have to put a cold rag on your head,
sing to you...

99
00:07:06,134 --> 00:07:08,303
...and apply VapoRub to your chest.

100
00:07:15,769 --> 00:07:19,314
You wanna rub something on my chest?

101
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:23,777
Yes. All over it.

102
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:29,324
Ahem. Maybe we should start with that.

103
00:07:31,326 --> 00:07:33,495
Now you're being a responsible patient.

104
00:07:44,381 --> 00:07:48,843
Now, you may notice some tingling.

105
00:07:49,219 --> 00:07:51,596
Oh, I'm counting on it.

106
00:07:53,807 --> 00:07:54,849
[SHELDON HUMMING]

107
00:07:58,395 --> 00:08:01,564
-Okay, dig in.
-Hold up.

108
00:08:03,692 --> 00:08:07,404
Bless us, O Lord, for these thy gifts
which we are about to receive...

109
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:10,407
...from thy bounty through Christ our Lord,
amen.

110
00:08:13,868 --> 00:08:15,704
Took the words right out of my mouth.

111
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:20,834
So, Dad, have you done any fishing lately?

112
00:08:21,042 --> 00:08:24,212
-I'm going next weekend.
-Oh. You like to fish?

113
00:08:25,255 --> 00:08:26,923
Yes.

114
00:08:29,718 --> 00:08:32,595
Sure. I can hear it in your voice.

115
00:08:33,555 --> 00:08:36,933
If he didn't like it, he wouldn't go.

116
00:08:39,102 --> 00:08:41,354
You know, I hadn't thought of that.

117
00:08:41,563 --> 00:08:43,356
[WHISPERS]
Help me.

118
00:08:45,233 --> 00:08:47,485
Dad, maybe you could take Howard
fishing sometime.

119
00:08:47,736 --> 00:08:52,407
-Give you a chance to get to know each other.
-No, no. We know each other well enough.

120
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:55,618
He's been talking my ear off all night.

121
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:58,163
Howie, I think you'd have fun.

122
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:04,961
-Fine. You can tag along.
BERNADETTE: Terrific.

123
00:09:05,128 --> 00:09:07,172
My two favorite fellas "gone fishing."

124
00:09:08,131 --> 00:09:11,885
Hang on a second.
Bernie, next weekend we have that thing.

125
00:09:12,093 --> 00:09:15,805
-What thing?
-You know, the thing.

126
00:09:16,639 --> 00:09:19,476
Oh, that thing. No, I canceled that thing.

127
00:09:21,478 --> 00:09:24,481
All right, it's settled.
You and I are going fishing.

128
00:09:24,647 --> 00:09:27,942
Great. Heh. Thanks for the help.

129
00:09:29,778 --> 00:09:32,822
I've never even been fishing.
This is gonna be a disaster.

130
00:09:33,031 --> 00:09:36,910
If you don't want to look foolish
doing something, you should practice.

131
00:09:37,118 --> 00:09:39,704
Do you know how many beef Wellingtons
I made by myself...

132
00:09:39,954 --> 00:09:41,790
...before I invited you guys over?

133
00:09:42,665 --> 00:09:49,005
I'll give you a hint.
You can see them here, here and here.

134
00:09:52,425 --> 00:09:55,345
Raj is right. You should get someone
to give you some pointers.

135
00:09:55,512 --> 00:09:57,138
Do you guys know how to fish?

136
00:09:57,639 --> 00:09:59,641
-No.
-No.

137
00:10:00,350 --> 00:10:04,312
But if you catch anything,
I know how to steam it in banana leaves.

138
00:10:05,313 --> 00:10:09,317
Come on, we must know somebody
who can do manly stuff like this.

139
00:10:12,654 --> 00:10:14,489
What's up?

140
00:10:18,409 --> 00:10:20,787
Step one, worms.

141
00:10:22,247 --> 00:10:23,289
Ew.

142
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:29,796
Okay, "ew" is one of the things you're not
gonna wanna say in front of your father-in-law.

143
00:10:30,046 --> 00:10:33,007
It's right up there with
"icky" and "get it away."

144
00:10:33,591 --> 00:10:36,386
-Now pick one up.
-Really?

145
00:10:36,594 --> 00:10:40,306
-You're gonna have to do it when you're fishing.
-Okay.

146
00:10:44,060 --> 00:10:45,228
What are you waiting for?

147
00:10:45,436 --> 00:10:48,439
I don't know.
For them to die of natural causes?

148
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:52,110
Just pick up a worm
and put him on this hook.

149
00:10:54,112 --> 00:10:55,530
Fine. Ahem.

150
00:10:56,948 --> 00:10:57,991
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

151
00:11:07,125 --> 00:11:08,251
There. Heh.

152
00:11:08,459 --> 00:11:12,755
I'm no expert, but I think the hook
has to go through the worm.

153
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:14,841
Fine.

154
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:17,093
Sorry, Mr. Worm.

155
00:11:17,302 --> 00:11:19,804
Sherm. Sherm the worm.

156
00:11:20,305 --> 00:11:23,099
Hey, don't name him,
just jab a hook in his face.

157
00:11:25,310 --> 00:11:27,770
-You got this, buddy.
-Yeah, come on. Hook that worm.

158
00:11:27,979 --> 00:11:30,106
-You can do it.
-That's great.

159
00:11:30,315 --> 00:11:32,066
Cheerleading. Way to man things up.

160
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:41,784
"--and the control group displayed
significantly fewer genetic abnormalities.

161
00:11:42,327 --> 00:11:45,288
But because of flaws
in the experimental design...

162
00:11:45,496 --> 00:11:47,706
...relating to environment and diet...

163
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:52,503
...they lived inconclusively ever after."
The end.

164
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:56,174
That was great. Rub my chest again.

165
00:11:56,341 --> 00:11:57,467
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

166
00:11:57,634 --> 00:11:59,677
No. I need to get you down for a nap.

167
00:11:59,844 --> 00:12:03,514
And for some reason,
that VapoRub gets you all fired up.

168
00:12:06,100 --> 00:12:09,896
-How's the poor thing?
-I'm hanging in there. Thanks for asking.

169
00:12:11,356 --> 00:12:14,525
Hey, Amy, I brought you some drugs
we've been working on in the lab.

170
00:12:14,692 --> 00:12:16,694
This is proving really good for congestion.

171
00:12:16,903 --> 00:12:19,322
There's a chance
it can make tears burn like acid.

172
00:12:19,530 --> 00:12:21,532
So if you take it, happy thoughts.

173
00:12:23,534 --> 00:12:25,870
I'm gonna draw you a soothing bath.

174
00:12:26,120 --> 00:12:29,499
-Where's your bath thermometer?
-I don't have a bath thermometer.

175
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:31,542
Fine, then I'm going to draw you...

176
00:12:31,709 --> 00:12:35,213
...a nerve-wracking bath
of indeterminate temperature.

177
00:12:36,755 --> 00:12:38,383
This is a really good expectorant.

178
00:12:38,549 --> 00:12:43,179
Although, some test subjects reported lactating
uncontrollably when they heard music.

179
00:12:44,389 --> 00:12:47,892
Okay, okay, here's the deal.
I don't need your medicine. I'm not sick.

180
00:12:48,268 --> 00:12:50,895
-I don't understand.
-I got better two days ago.

181
00:12:51,729 --> 00:12:54,440
It's just been so nice
having Sheldon take care of me.

182
00:12:54,691 --> 00:12:59,570
-So you've just been lying to him?
-You see the stuff in my nose? Rubber cement.

183
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:05,910
I don't mean to be judgy,
but this is the kind of thing lunatics do.

184
00:13:07,578 --> 00:13:10,373
All right. I'll tell him.

185
00:13:10,581 --> 00:13:15,295
SHELDON: Amy, would you be strong enough
to bathe yourself or do you need my help?

186
00:13:19,424 --> 00:13:20,591
I'll tell him tomorrow.

187
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:24,679
Momma needs a bath.

188
00:13:27,557 --> 00:13:30,727
Now, let's assume by some miracle
you actually catch a fish.

189
00:13:30,935 --> 00:13:34,105
You're gonna have to know how to gut it.
So, what you're gonna do...

190
00:13:34,605 --> 00:13:38,484
...is you're gonna take your knife,
slice him right up the belly.

191
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:39,694
[GAGS]

192
00:13:42,780 --> 00:13:45,116
-Do you want me to stop?
-No, I'm fine. Keep going.

193
00:13:45,325 --> 00:13:49,620
You don't wanna cut too deep into his guts
or the blood will just squirt all over your face.

194
00:13:49,787 --> 00:13:50,829
[ALL GAG]

195
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:56,419
Oh, my God. What is with you guys?

196
00:13:56,627 --> 00:14:00,214
Well, it's not our fault.
Our dads never did anything like this with us.

197
00:14:00,423 --> 00:14:03,259
-What, never?
-My dad was an anthropologist.

198
00:14:03,468 --> 00:14:05,136
The only father-son time he spent...

199
00:14:05,303 --> 00:14:09,098
...was with a 2000-year-old skeleton
of an Etruscan boy.

200
00:14:09,807 --> 00:14:11,309
I hated that kid.

201
00:14:13,144 --> 00:14:15,646
Mine just took me to his gynecology office.

202
00:14:15,854 --> 00:14:19,150
I got so bored, I'd put vaginal lubricant
at the bottom of my shoes...

203
00:14:19,359 --> 00:14:21,944
...and pretend I was ice skating.

204
00:14:26,324 --> 00:14:29,494
Yeah, well my quality father-son time
was spending my adolescence...

205
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:33,872
...looking out the window,
waiting for my dad to come back some day.

206
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,460
Yeah, okay, Howard wins.

207
00:14:38,836 --> 00:14:41,881
We didn't have opportunities like this
when we were growing up...

208
00:14:42,131 --> 00:14:45,885
...but right now there's a dad
that wants to take you on a fishing trip.

209
00:14:46,177 --> 00:14:48,638
You're right. Ugh. I should do this.

210
00:14:48,846 --> 00:14:50,848
Great. Ahem. Here you go.

211
00:14:51,015 --> 00:14:55,561
Now what you do is, you stick your thumb
down its throat, grab the guts and pull.

212
00:14:59,482 --> 00:15:01,192
Here we go.

213
00:15:04,362 --> 00:15:05,405
[GROANING]

214
00:15:06,364 --> 00:15:09,075
Oh, look, it's a female.
You can see all the eggs.

215
00:15:09,242 --> 00:15:10,284
[ALL GAG]

216
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:17,417
[KATRINA AND THE WAVES' "WALKING ON
SUNSHINE" PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]

217
00:15:22,547 --> 00:15:23,840
[CLICKS]

218
00:15:28,719 --> 00:15:31,722
Oh, Sheldon, am I glad you're back.

219
00:15:31,889 --> 00:15:34,308
I've taken a turn for the worst.

220
00:15:35,226 --> 00:15:37,728
I think I'm gonna need another bath.

221
00:15:39,188 --> 00:15:40,731
I'm surprised to hear that.

222
00:15:40,898 --> 00:15:44,610
You see, the other day,
I was concerned that you weren't recovering...

223
00:15:44,861 --> 00:15:47,238
...so while you were sleeping,
I took a cheek swab...

224
00:15:47,447 --> 00:15:49,115
...and had it cultured in the lab.

225
00:15:50,241 --> 00:15:52,326
-Oh?
-I got the results back.

226
00:15:52,535 --> 00:15:55,455
Have you developed any
of the following symptoms?

227
00:15:55,705 --> 00:16:02,086
A growing nose or perhaps a warm sensation
in the trouser region?

228
00:16:02,753 --> 00:16:06,591
Also known as full-blown
Liar, Liar, Pants on Fire.

229
00:16:07,258 --> 00:16:10,595
All right, all right.
But I really was sick at the beginning.

230
00:16:10,845 --> 00:16:13,973
It's just been so nice
having you take care of me.

231
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:18,060
It hurts that you would lie to me, Amy.

232
00:16:18,269 --> 00:16:20,938
I thought our relationship
was based on trust...

233
00:16:21,105 --> 00:16:25,151
...and a mutual admiration
that skews in my favor.

234
00:16:25,943 --> 00:16:27,570
I feel terrible I did this.

235
00:16:27,778 --> 00:16:31,949
It pains me to say it,
but I think some form of penalty is in order...

236
00:16:32,116 --> 00:16:35,495
...so as to discourage this type of behavior
in the future.

237
00:16:35,745 --> 00:16:38,498
I suppose that's fair. What do you suggest?

238
00:16:38,748 --> 00:16:42,919
In a perfect world, I'd lock you in a stockade
in the public square.

239
00:16:43,503 --> 00:16:46,088
And that probably requires a permit.

240
00:16:48,633 --> 00:16:52,428
I could not be allowed to go to the opening
of the next Star Trek movie.

241
00:16:52,637 --> 00:16:55,640
Oh, that seems overly harsh.

242
00:16:56,516 --> 00:16:59,519
You gave in to a human weakness.
You didn't kill a man.

243
00:17:00,311 --> 00:17:03,773
You know, it's a tad old-school...

244
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:06,651
...but my father was not one
to spare the rod...

245
00:17:06,901 --> 00:17:11,322
...when my brother would sneak into his truck
and drink his driving whiskey.

246
00:17:13,824 --> 00:17:16,953
Are you saying you wanna spank me?

247
00:17:19,330 --> 00:17:21,916
I don't want to...

248
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:25,836
...but it looks like you left me no choice.

249
00:17:28,506 --> 00:17:29,924
That's true.

250
00:17:33,177 --> 00:17:36,305
I've been a very bad girl.

251
00:17:40,518 --> 00:17:42,520
Hi-ho, hi-ho, it's off to fish we go.

252
00:17:44,855 --> 00:17:47,024
-That's what you're wearing?
-No good?

253
00:17:47,233 --> 00:17:50,987
The guy at the sporting goods store
said these are what fishermen wear.

254
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:53,531
Maybe in cartoons.

255
00:17:55,032 --> 00:17:59,203
I wish I had known that before
I posted all those pictures on Facebook.

256
00:18:01,706 --> 00:18:05,543
All right. Let's hit the road. I wouldn't mind
shooting some ducks in the morning.

257
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:08,087
Wait, now we're shooting things?

258
00:18:09,046 --> 00:18:10,965
I like using a big shell.

259
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:14,468
You can't eat them afterwards
but it's fun watching them blow up.

260
00:18:19,181 --> 00:18:25,354
Sir, I'm flattered that you invited me
and I really want you to like me...

261
00:18:25,563 --> 00:18:30,901
...but I don't think this trip is the way to do it.

262
00:18:32,028 --> 00:18:35,698
And I can't return these things
if there's chunks of duck all over them.

263
00:18:36,115 --> 00:18:40,077
-So why'd you agree to come?
-Because Bernadette made me.

264
00:18:40,286 --> 00:18:44,582
I tried to back out too.
My wife said I had to go.

265
00:18:44,790 --> 00:18:49,045
Really? Your wife makes you do stuff?
You're a big, scary cop.

266
00:18:49,712 --> 00:18:52,256
You're an astronaut
and your wife makes you do things...

267
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:55,259
...and she's only 4 feet tall.

268
00:18:58,638 --> 00:19:03,392
So, what do we do now?
They expect us to go away for the weekend.

269
00:19:05,895 --> 00:19:06,937
[SIGHS]

270
00:19:09,315 --> 00:19:12,943
There's an Indian casino near Palm Springs.

271
00:19:14,445 --> 00:19:16,405
You know how to shoot craps?

272
00:19:16,614 --> 00:19:19,075
No, but I'm not a stranger to dice games.

273
00:19:19,283 --> 00:19:22,536
I was the Temple Beth-El Hebrew School
Yahtzee champion.

274
00:19:24,872 --> 00:19:25,915
[SPEAKS IN HEBREW]

275
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:30,127
I'll teach you how to play.

276
00:19:31,295 --> 00:19:33,130
Really?

277
00:19:33,923 --> 00:19:35,257
Thank you, sir.

278
00:19:37,134 --> 00:19:38,636
Call me Mike.

279
00:19:40,971 --> 00:19:42,348
Okay.

280
00:19:45,643 --> 00:19:49,605
Boy, we're just married to
a couple of ball-busters, huh, Mike?

281
00:19:51,148 --> 00:19:53,984
That's my wife and daughter
you're talking about.

282
00:19:56,654 --> 00:19:58,614
Great couple of gals.

283
00:19:59,490 --> 00:20:00,825
I wouldn't go that far.

284
00:20:06,789 --> 00:20:08,791
Are you prepared to receive
your punishment?

285
00:20:12,962 --> 00:20:15,881
One second. I wanna put on some music.

286
00:20:17,383 --> 00:20:18,884
Why?

287
00:20:19,135 --> 00:20:22,805
I don't wanna disturb the people next door
while you discipline me.

288
00:20:24,432 --> 00:20:25,766
[SOUL MUSIC PLAYING OVER SPEAKERS]

289
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:33,065
Very well, then.
Get over my knee. Let's begin.

290
00:20:40,072 --> 00:20:41,824
Oh, my.

291
00:20:42,241 --> 00:20:46,245
Excuse me. You're not supposed
to be enjoying this.

292
00:20:46,954 --> 00:20:49,665
Then maybe you should spank me harder.

293
00:20:52,835 --> 00:20:54,920
Maybe I will.

294
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:57,423
[AMY GIGGLES]

